---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Who runs Cascadia Systems, how it started as a mapping lab, and how I work — Devin MacArthur, Portland, Oregon"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero-topo section bg-gradient-to-b from-dark-bg via-dark-surface to-dark-bg">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h1 class="mb-8 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Who I am</h1>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            I'm Devin MacArthur. I live in East Portland and I've spent the last few years as the
            data-systems person at a statewide membership organization, which is a job title that
            means "the one who makes the systems talk to each other." The CRM is Salesforce with a
            lot of custom objects. Under it is an older membership database that everything still
            depends on. Around them are SharePoint, a payment processor, an election platform, and
            the spreadsheets that hold an organization together whether anyone admits it or not.
          </p>
          <p>
            Most of what I've built there began as somebody's weekly chore. A snapshot of the
            whole membership every morning at 6:30, because the questions people asked on Tuesday
            couldn't be answered from Friday's data. A map of which field staff cover which local
            units, because the answer used to live in one person's head. An extractor for scanned
            applications. A reconciliation that caught a payment outage nobody upstream had
            reported. The pattern is the same each time: find the person doing the tedious
            thing, understand exactly what they're checking for, and then make the computer check
            it every night.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How it started -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">How this company started, and why it changed</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            I registered Cascadia Mobile Research LLC in March 2026 as a drone and LiDAR mapping
            lab. I still have the drone, the scanner, and the GPU workstation that processes the
            scans, and the mapping work was interesting. But the thing people kept
            actually asking me for, once they knew what I did all day, was the data work. So in
            September I stopped pretending the company was about aircraft. Cascadia Systems is
            the same LLC pointed at the work I'm good at. The old site is archived, not deleted;
            if you came here for photogrammetry, email me anyway and I'll tell you what I can and
            can't do.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- How I work -->
  <section class="section bg-dark-surface">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">How I work</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            I start by interviewing, not by reading requirements. The procedure document says
            what the process is supposed to be; the person doing it knows the four exceptions
            that make it take twice as long. I build for the exceptions.
          </p>
          <p>
            I don't deliver prototypes. If I show you something running, it is running on a
            schedule with logs, and there's a written procedure for the day it fails. I take
            that seriously because I once watched a vendor's outage go unnoticed for six weeks,
            and the only reason it was noticed at all was a check that happened to be running.
          </p>
          <p>
            I write everything down as I go, partly because that's how I think and partly because
            I'm one person and the documentation is the only thing that makes it safe to hire one
            person. Outside of work I write essays about institutions and measurement at
            <a href="https://devinmacarthur.substack.com" class="link" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Systems Inquiry</a>,
            which will tell you more about how I think than this page can.
          </p>
          <p>
            I have graduate training in urban studies at Portland State. It's where I learned to
            distrust summary statistics, which turns out to be most of the job.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Business -->
  <section class="section border-t border-dark-border">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl">
        <h2 class="mb-6 text-3xl font-bold">The business, plainly</h2>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-secondary">
          <p>
            Cascadia Systems is the practice of Cascadia Mobile Research LLC, an Oregon company.
            It's one person, taking one or two engagements at a time.
            There is no investor, no growth target, and no plan to become an agency. I'd like it
            to still exist in ten years, doing roughly this, a little better each year.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row">
          <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary">Email me</a>
          <a href="/services/" class="btn btn-secondary">What I do</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
